Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:26:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/44] inventory: the client moves items to and from node
 inventories at once

Moving an item between the player's inventory and a chest's (or a furnace's) only showed once the server
answered: the client predicts a move only when both sides are the player's own inventory. Dropped on the
other side, the item went back to its slot until then, and on a busy server (a new world saving its
generated blocks takes the server's step past a second on a slow device) it blinked there for as long.

A node's inventory is predicted too now. The server always sends the node's metadata and the player's
affected lists again after a move, before any check, so when it refuses one (a callback allowing less, too
far away) the guess is put right. Detached inventories stay as before: they are sent again only when they
change, and some hand out items without losing them (creative).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/inventorymanager.cpp b/src/inventorymanager.cpp
index 7f473a6b8..752b8308d 100644
--- a/src/inventorymanager.cpp
+++ b/src/inventorymanager.cpp
@@ -628,7 +628,12 @@ void IMoveAction::clientApply(InventoryManager *mgr, IGameDef *gamedef)
 	InventoryLocation current_player;
 	current_player.setCurrentPlayer();
 	Inventory *inv_player = mgr->getInventory(current_player);
-	if (inv_from != inv_player || inv_to != inv_player)
+	// A node's inventory too: the server sends its metadata and the player's list again after every move
+	// (see Server::handleCommand_InventoryAction), so a guess its callbacks refuse is put right
+	auto predicted = [&](const InventoryLocation &loc, Inventory *inv) {
+		return inv == inv_player || loc.type == InventoryLocation::NODEMETA;
+	};
+	if (!predicted(from_inv, inv_from) || !predicted(to_inv, inv_to))
 		return;
 
 	InventoryList *list_from = inv_from->getList(from_list);
